        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0755be81-c1b5-5e4c-a6c8-ef6db52e8e58",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, Virginia 529 College Savings 250\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Topics: NASCAR race sponsorship, essay contest naming\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- From 2007 to 2011, former title sponsor Crown Royal named the Toyota Owners 400 after the winner of an essay contest during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway Cup Series races, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring.\n- The Virginia 529 College Savings 250 is held the night before the Federated Auto Parts 400.",
